{"title":"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Ricky Liu</i>) Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e4194d33d81c3dd5ac49c773335504c4a7a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> positive rational numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8c97f116608cdd31187eeb9b47a0adbd951c41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"11\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2364974bb35189a09a0170ded45791f8b62ce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_k = a_1\\cdot a_2\\cdots a_k = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"291\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First, consider composite numbers.  We can then factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e1024eb8ee840755146659a9475d8a1230b50f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1p_2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"11\" />  It is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/0/7e0ec4001b6e984971c53090ffe0d25d7b23894f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1+p_2\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />, and thus, we can add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/4523cd45f32b9357272ca3a6c1e6dd55499824f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-p_1-p_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> 1s in order to achieve a sum and product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22d9030fd69b27ce266431c2e185538f3951471f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1+p_2=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, which is only possible in one case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, we consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b5aef17fa0cdfbda2068d67d1601126dc331723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1=p_2=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />.  \n</p><p>Secondly, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a prime.  Then we can find the following procedure: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/9117b42526dcfd8b73dcb6edfde24c80928130f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\frac{n}{2}, a_2=4, a_3=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"175\" height=\"37\" /> and let the rest of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> be 1.  The only numbers we now need to check are those such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02da0e1b19e8f97b0f761ad533af3f7ae9874e5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{2}+4+\\frac{1}{2}&gt;n\\Longrightarrow n&lt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"199\" height=\"37\" />.  Thus, we need to check for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d780d48b062a164c391eb6ddbf071bccf42ede95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1,2,3,5,7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" />.  One is included because it is neither prime nor composite.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cf2183727a4cc5818b2c4c94f0a0f0000f1be9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1a_2\\hdots a_k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />.  Then by AM-GM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/2/f222225a093b7e48e59c9c594b7380a08e201894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+\\hdots+a_k\\ge k\\sqrt[k]{1}&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"232\" height=\"19\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e4194d33d81c3dd5ac49c773335504c4a7a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is impossible.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, once again consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/506947498c395d57c1a4eb6430db08b584862ee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1a_2\\hdots a_k=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />.  Similar to the above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd202c264c3fcb5346fc397c670051400ab52cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+\\hdots\\ge k\\sqrt[k]{2}&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"192\" height=\"19\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e4194d33d81c3dd5ac49c773335504c4a7a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/976a0cdd79a56bc50b9ae51f2c51f1c2d2a7ff4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[k]{2}&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c877cdefa36f90cdf80f93dadc93cc77d19961a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is then impossible.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/88697b6188ff310991627adbc3f5829165ed4684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1a_2\\hdots a_k=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />.  Again, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11c2035339882294bf977c75649937e20911285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+\\hdots\\ge k\\sqrt[k]{3}&gt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"192\" height=\"19\" />.  This is obvious for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74fde52e795da2282474f9e58e6ea929b5da9279.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  Now consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e537cc8b984599bf7996da8fcbba69950721a7e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{3}\\approx 3.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> is obviously greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is impossible.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, proceed as above and consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8205f912abb8a61a6d8a5a49dcad94ec6750cd55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4ac82649c3c1e5e8c2aa4081e2c1646c16380541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1a_2=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />.  However, we then come to the quadratic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/80458cf8b3225eb99ae00f0caec7af66aa51a330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^2-5a_1+5=0 \\Longrightarrow a_1=\\frac{5\\pm\\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"269\" height=\"41\" />, which is not rational.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eeae143c5c9dbd376ffa1ffa8bdb93a58e8c9889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a98580fcc6706b5b71f59256675cecaa87bfc64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3]{5}&gt;\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38bbb4ead2b912c0052298f2baf91003236e5c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[4]{5}&gt;\\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" />.  This is trivial to prove.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c050157e825ba04978b0e5ebd7cad1e6e9487f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, it is obviously impossible, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> does not work.\n</p><p>The last case, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f0f830b5b25ea929198068e407e8c9f62f56c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, is possible using the following three numbers.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac97b127c5d8875f5ff4704e3d7c27091fdde7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\frac{9}{2}, a_2=\\frac{4}{3}, a_3=\\frac{7}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"177\" height=\"37\" /> shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f0f830b5b25ea929198068e407e8c9f62f56c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is possible.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can be any positive integer greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with the exclusion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?t=84554 Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO\" title=\"2006 USAMO\">2006 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017095441\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 323/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1663/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9746/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   19.822      1 -total\n 40.03%    7.934      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 30.82%    6.110      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 27.84%    5.519      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3187:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017095441 and revision id 62762. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}